,"name":"Reviews inbox: thread sheet","spec":{"accessibility":["The slide-over and the sheet are labelled dialogs with a visible Close button; focus moves to the title on open and back to the row on close.","Phone controls are 44px targets and the reply is 16px text so iOS does not zoom; status is a glyph with its word.","Resolve names what it does through the line under it; a refusal is text, never only a disabled button."],"constraints":["Built only from Adapter Widgets (Stack, Text, Button, Badge, Icon, TextInput, TimelineItem, Alert, Sheet, Disclosure); no Widget outside the Adapter catalog.","The Variants change the thread and the member; the slide-over and the sheet are told apart by the viewport of the render context (responsive layout), not by a Variant.","The strings of the app are copied under the same Locale keys; names and ids bind through value and value2. en-US and zh-TW keep identical key sets.","Buttons are 28px on the slide-over and 40px on the sheet (touch targets are 44px in the app); the drag of the sheet is not modelled. The thread is a Sheet (the dim layer behind it is part of the Widget), whose footer holds the reply and lifecycle rows. The queue behind the overlay is the sibling queue View.","Visual language follows the Quiet Canvas design system in DESIGN.md."],"decisions":[],"entryConditions":["A member selected a row of the Reviews queue on a tablet or a phone, or followed a thread link there; the thread opens over the queue and closing it returns to the queue with focus on the row.","The render context selects the viewport: at the tablet width the thread is a slide-over from the right, at the phone width a bottom sheet with a grab handle; each hides what its footer does not offer. The base state is an open thread read by a member who may reply and resolve.","The render context also selects one Locale and one theme; the strings follow the Workbench language and names and ids are literal identities."],"intent":"Show how a thread of the Reviews inbox opens below the desktop layout: the slide-over of a tablet and the bottom sheet of a phone, where a reviewer reads, replies, resolves and reopens, and the notice above the queue when a linked thread does not exist.","interactionRules":["The header names the thread, its status, View and target, and has the thread menu and Close; the slide-over also offers Open in canvas. The sheet is named by the thread title and takes focus on it, never on the reply box, so the keyboard does not rise on its own.","The reply box sends with the send button on a phone (a full Reply button with ⌘↵ on the slide-over). Resolve is one tap: it answers an open thread, and on a ready-for-review thread the slide-over reads Accept and resolve while the sheet keeps Resolve; the line under it says what it does and which submission it accepts.","A ready or resolved thread offers Reopen (beside Resolve on a ready one, alone on a resolved one); a resolved thread has no reply box. On a phone neither the sheet nor its menu offers Re-anchor, Promote to Decision or Submit for review.","A member who may not reply reads the thread and \"You can read this thread, but not reply to it or change its status.\" Below the desktop layout a link to a thread this Workspace does not have shows a notice above the queue with Dismiss."],"references":[{"label":"Phase 5 of the closed loop: dogfood coverage of the core surfaces","relation":"decision","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/discussions/379#discussioncomment-19257377"},{"relation":"sibling","type":"view","viewId":"468247e8-4f39-4f04-8056-b2af4c1c37ea"},{"relation":"sibling","type":"view","viewId":"c6c0a104-7b3e-4d19-8a26-3e9d1c0b6a04"},{"relation":"sibling","type":"view","viewId":"c6c0a101-7b3e-4d19-8a26-3e9d1c0b6a01"},{"relation":"sibling","type":"view","viewId":"e1b7a101-4c2d-4e3f-9a5b-6d7c8e9f0a01"},{"relation":"sibling","type":"view","viewId":"e1b7a102-4c2d-4e3f-9a5b-6d7c8e9f0a02"},{"relation":"sibling","type":"view","viewId":"e1b7a103-4c2d-4e3f-9a5b-6d7c8e9f0a03"},{"relation":"sibling","type":"view","viewId":"e1b7a104-4c2d-4e3f-9a5b-6d7c8e9f0a04"},{"relation":"sibling","type":"view","viewId":"e1b7a105-4c2d-4e3f-9a5b-6d7c8e9f0a05"}],"requirements":["01a116f0-9170-72ca-872c-a9ca805fc8e1","01a116f0-9128-77b3-8800-1a9edf67106c"]},"variants":{"read-only":{"state":{"ft-sheet":{"visible":false},"ft-slide":{"visible":false},"ro-note":{"visible":true}}},"ready-for-review":{"requirements":["01a116f0-9170-72ca-872c-a9ca805fc8e1"],"state":{"bd-open":{"visible":false},"bd-ready":{"visible":true},"fh-h-accepts":{"visible":true},"fh-h-answers":{"visible":false},"fh-reopen-cell":{"visible":true},"fs-accept":{"visible":true},"fs-h-accepts":{"visible":true},"fs-h-answers":{"visible":false},"fs-reopen":{"visible":true},"fs-resolve":{"visible":false},"sub-current":{"visible":true}}},"resolved":{"requirements":["01a116f0-9170-72ca-872c-a9ca805fc8e1"],"state":{"bd-open":{"visible":false},"bd-resolved":{"visible":true},"fh-h-answers":{"visible":false},"fh-reopen-cell":{"visible":true},"fh-reply-row":{"visible":false},"fh-split":{"visible":false},"fs-h-answers":{"visible":false},"fs-reopen":{"visible":true},"fs-reply-btn-wrap":{"visible":false},"fs-reply-wrap":{"visible":false},"fs-resolve":{"visible":false},"fs-split":{"visible":false},"res-answered":{"visible":true},"rs-answered":{"visible":true}}},"thread-missing":{"requirements":["01a11544-5b42-7ca4-a501-a1c4977a6ccd"],"state":{"list-card-wrap":{"visible":true},"ov":{"visible":false}}}}}
